---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PawIcon from '../components/PawIcon.astro'

// Kept deliberately short. The substance — process, AI disclosure, what we
// don't do, how the money works — lives on /how-we-pick/ so there's exactly
// one page to keep honest, rather than two that drift apart. This page is the
// personality; that page is the contract.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Shopping Sloth"
  description="Who runs Shopping Sloth, what we publish, and why we're upfront about being an affiliate site that doesn't test products."
>
  <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:760px;">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <PawIcon size={12} />
        about us
      </div>
      <h1>Slow picks. Fast results.</h1>
    </div>

    <p>
      Here's the thing about sloths: they move at about 0.15 miles per hour. They sleep up to 15 hours a
      day. They will not be rushed.
    </p>
    <p>
      But sloths are also incredibly deliberate. Every move they make is efficient, necessary, and
      considered. If a sloth is going somewhere, it's going somewhere good. That's basically our whole
      editorial philosophy.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      Shopping Sloth is a small independent affiliate site publishing buying-guide roundups — "best
      X" lists, five picks at a time, in categories like home, tech, health, and accessories. We started
      it because most roundups in this genre read like nobody involved got past the first review, and we
      thought a slower one would be more useful.
    </p>

    <h2 id="editor">Who writes this</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are published under the Shopping Sloth editorial team rather than a personal byline,
      because that's accurate: roundups are drafted with AI research grounded in published reviews, then
      checked and edited by a person before anything goes live. We'd rather tell you that than invent a
      masthead.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not a testing lab, a retailer, or a manufacturer. We don't handle the products we write
      about — we read the people who do, and we cite them on each article.
      <a href="/how-we-pick/">Here's the full process, in detail.</a>
    </p>

    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>
      Some links are affiliate links, and as an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases made
      through them, at no extra cost to you. We also run display ads. No brand pays to be featured or
      ranked here. <a href="/how-we-pick/#how-we-make-money">More on that.</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Tell us when we're wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Discontinued pick, dead link, a claim that doesn't hold up? Email
      <a href="mailto:hello@shoppingsloth.com">hello@shoppingsloth.com</a>. We fix things and date the
      fix. See also our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="quote" style="margin:56px 0;">
      <p>"We move slow, but only toward the good stuff."</p>
      <span>— the shopping sloth team</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
